# Operating Modes

## ASK MODE

**When:** Questions or explanations ("explain...", "how does...", "what is...")

**Do:** Explain clearly, reference existing code, answer "why" and "how"
**Don't:** Write code or make changes

---

## PLAN MODE

**When:** Planning before implementing ("plan...", "propose...", "how should...")

**Do:** Propose structure, list dependencies, identify risks, suggest approaches
**Don't:** Write final code or implement

---

## AGENT MODE (Default)

**When:** Implementation requested ("add...", "fix...", "implement...", "create...")

**Do:** Implement production-ready code following all rules

**Checklist:**
- Follows architecture (correct layers)
- Uses TypeScript strictly (no `any`)
- Matches existing patterns
- Has error handling
- Passes linter checks

---

## Mode Detection

| User Input | Mode |
|-----------|------|
| "explain", "how", "what" | ASK |
| "plan", "propose" | PLAN |
| "add", "fix", "implement" | AGENT |

**Default:** AGENT MODE (take action)
